{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774169453,"nonce":"KR7kQb/V3jCyas41bI7tDxD711g=","title":"Add `nightshift issue` CLI passthrough to tracker","message":"## Problem\n\nDirect `git-bug` CLI calls hit lock contention with the watcher. The lock retry logic in `GitBugTracker._run()` only protects calls through the adapter.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nAdd `nightshift issue ...` where everything after `issue` is passed literally to the tracker CLI. For git-bug, `nightshift issue bug show abc` runs `git-bug bug show abc` through the adapter's `_run()`, getting lock retry for free.\n\nImplementation: `cmd_issue` in `cli.py` instantiates the tracker, calls a new `run_raw(*args)` method that passes args straight to `_run()`. Thin passthrough — no argument parsing, no mapping.\n\n## Benefits\n- Lock contention solved for all callers\n- Tracker-agnostic (future adapters implement `run_raw` differently)\n- No need to maintain a mapping of subcommands\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `nightshift issue bug show \u003cid\u003e` works like `git-bug bug show \u003cid\u003e` but with retry\n- [ ] `nightshift issue push` works like `git-bug push` but with retry\n- [ ] All args after `issue` passed literally to tracker\n- [ ] Lock retry applies to all calls\n- [ ] Tests for passthrough dispatch\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md updated","files":null}]}